{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.S5SO3FiberAction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Group.List.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":115,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.trace_factorization_closure","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.trace_factorization_closure","kind":"theorem","line":868,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L868-L868","doc":"**Substantive**: The physical mass gap equals the product of the raw \nstructural scale and the exact left cell Betti sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.target_binding_gap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.target_binding_gap","kind":"def","line":864,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L864-L864","doc":"The target experimental A=4 binding energy (28.30 MeV). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.betti_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.betti_sum","kind":"def","line":861,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L861-L861","doc":"The exact Kazhdan-Lusztig Betti sum for the A=4 left cell. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.raw_structural_scale","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.raw_structural_scale","kind":"def","line":858,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L858-L858","doc":"The raw (unweighted) structural scale of the trace (e.g. `~0.0059 MeV`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization.mk","kind":"ctor","line":856,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L856-L856","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A4BettiTraceFactorization","kind":"class","line":848,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L848-L869","doc":"**Class: A=4 Trace Factorization over Hecke Left Cells.**\n\nThe conjectural physical closure: the Hecke mass element trace is precisely \nfactorized into a base structural scale times the Kazhdan-Lusztig geometric \nrepresentation weight (the Betti sum over the canonical left cell $C_\\\\lambda$).\n\nThis provides the mathematical scaffold for the Option E closure at A=4, \ncarried as a class field per AGENTS.md §3b-cond. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.leftCellBettiSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.leftCellBettiSum","kind":"def","line":840,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L840-L846","doc":"The exact Betti sum over the canonical left cell $C_\\\\lambda$ corresponding\nto the A=4 partition (e.g., $\\\\lambda = (10, 2)$).\nEvaluated by summing the Kazhdan-Lusztig polynomials at $q=1$. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_irrep_class_duality","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_irrep_class_duality","kind":"theorem","line":815,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L815-L828","doc":"The character-table pairing is a bijection: injective (distinct irreps ↦\ndistinct classes) and surjective (every class is hit).  This is the\nirrep ↔ conjugacy-class duality the fiber map realizes — the structural\ntarget named by `five_distinct_classes`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5IrrepToClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5IrrepToClass","kind":"def","line":797,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L797-L813","doc":"**Character-table duality (the 5 ↔ 5 bijection).** A complete character\ntheory pairs the five A₅ irreps with the five conjugacy classes via a square\ncharacter table.  We name the canonical diagonal pairing\n(A ↔ id, T₁ ↔ fiveCycleA, T₂ ↔ fiveCycleB, G ↔ threeCycle, H ↔\ndoubleTransp) and prove it is a BIJECTION — the explicit codomain structure\nbehind `BringFiberAction.five_distinct_classes`.\n\nThe T₁/T₂ ↔ fiveCycleA/fiveCycleB assignment is forced by chirality: the\ntwo faithful 3-dim irreps are distinguished exactly by their values on the\ntwo 5-cycle classes (χ_{T₁}(5A) = φ, χ_{T₂}(5A) = φ̄ = 1−φ, swapped on 5B),\nso the chirality pair of irreps pairs with the chirality pair of classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_fivecycle_chirality_pair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_fivecycle_chirality_pair","kind":"theorem","line":787,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L787-L795","doc":"**The 5-cycle classes are the chirality pair** (same size, same element\norder, distinct classes).  This is the class-side face of the T₁/T₂ split:\nthe two enantiomorphic 5-cycle classes are exchanged by the S₅∖A₅ parity,\nexactly as T₁ ↔ T₂ are (cf. `s5_to_a5_electron_block_splits`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_class_sizes_sum_60","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_class_sizes_sum_60","kind":"theorem","line":781,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L781-L785","doc":"**Class sizes partition |A₅| = 60** (the orbit-counting / class-equation\nbackbone): 1 + 15 + 20 + 12 + 12 = 60.  Confirms the five classes are a\ncomplete partition of the group. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_classes_eq_irreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_classes_eq_irreps","kind":"theorem","line":773,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L773-L779","doc":"**Class-count = irrep-count = 5 (the character-table is square).** A₅ has\nexactly five conjugacy classes, matching its five irreps (`A5Irrep`).  This\nsquareness is precisely the duality the fiber map realizes: the five A₅\nirreps map injectively onto the five conjugacy classes (the codomain of\n`BringFiberAction.five_distinct_classes`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.elementOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.elementOrder","kind":"def","line":768,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L768-L771","doc":"Order of a representative element of each class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.size","kind":"def","line":763,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L763-L766","doc":"Size of each A₅ conjugacy class. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.allList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.allList","kind":"def","line":759,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L759-L761","doc":"All five A₅ conjugacy classes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5ConjClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5ConjClass","kind":"instance","line":757,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L757-L757","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5ConjClass.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5ConjClass.repr","kind":"def","line":757,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L757-L757","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqA5ConjClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqA5ConjClass","kind":"instance","line":757,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L757-L757","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.fiveCycleB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.fiveCycleB","kind":"ctor","line":756,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L756-L756","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.fiveCycleA","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.fiveCycleA","kind":"ctor","line":755,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L755-L755","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.threeCycle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.threeCycle","kind":"ctor","line":754,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L754-L754","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.doubleTransp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.doubleTransp","kind":"ctor","line":753,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L753-L753","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass.id","kind":"ctor","line":752,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L752-L752","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5ConjClass","kind":"inductive","line":748,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L748-L757","doc":"The five conjugacy classes of A₅ ≅ I (icosahedral rotation group):\nidentity, double-transpositions, 3-cycles, and the two enantiomorphic\n5-cycle classes (swapped by the S₅∖A₅ parity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopf_selection_dims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopf_selection_dims","kind":"theorem","line":716,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L716-L722","doc":"**The selected irrep has the expected dimension.** The electron generation\n(ℓ=1 → T₁) is 3-dimensional (the chiral color sheets), and the muon\ngeneration (ℓ=2 → H) is 5-dimensional.  Confirms the selection map lands on\nthe irreps whose dimensions match the corpus generation assignment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopf_generation_selection","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopf_generation_selection","kind":"theorem","line":693,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L693-L714","doc":"**Hopf selection theorem (combinatorial leg).** The generation-selection map\nreads off `icosBranchingMult`: at ℓ=1 the unique nonzero multiplicity is the\nT₁ slot (electron), and at ℓ=2 it is the H slot (muon).  Concretely the\nselected irrep's slot carries multiplicity 1 while the *other* generation's\nslot is 0 at that level — so the two generations are cleanly separated by ℓ.\n\nThe four equalities verify, against the raw `icosBranchingMult` table:\n(i)  ℓ=1 selects T₁ — its T₁-slot (index 1) is 1;\n(ii) ℓ=1 does NOT yet see H — its H-slot (index 4) is 0;\n(iii) ℓ=2 selects H — its H-slot (index 4) is 1;\n(iv) ℓ=2 does NOT carry T₁ — its T₁-slot (index 1) is 0.\nHence `hopfGenerationSelect 1 = T₁` and `hopfGenerationSelect 2 = H` are\nthe correct combinatorial targets the Hopf moment map (#2370) realizes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopfGenerationSelect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.hopfGenerationSelect","kind":"def","line":684,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L684-L691","doc":"The Hopf generation-selection map: the A₅ irrep singled out at spherical-\nharmonic level ℓ as its lowest-ℓ (first-appearing) icosahedral content.\nℓ=1 → T₁ (electron), ℓ=2 → H (muon).  Index into `IcosahedralIrrepDims`\nordering [A, T₁, T₂, G, H]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_a5_electron_block_splits","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_a5_electron_block_splits","kind":"theorem","line":654,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L654-L664","doc":"**S₅ ↓ A₅ on the self-conjugate (3,1,1) block.**  V_(3,1,1) is\nself-conjugate (`conjugate` fixes it), restricts non-trivially to A₅\n(`restrictsToA5Irrep = true`), and its dim 6 splits as the chirality\npair T₁ ⊕ T₂ (3 + 3) swapped by the S₅∖A₅ parity.  The self-conjugacy\n(= invariance under the sign-twist) is exactly the structural reason\nthe block carries the chirality (cf. `PartitionOf5.electron_block`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.so3_to_a5_irrep_content","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.so3_to_a5_irrep_content","kind":"theorem","line":641,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L641-L652","doc":"**SO(3) ↓ A₅ irrep content at low ℓ.**  Read directly off\n`icosBranchingMult` against the irrep ordering [A, T₁, T₂, G, H]\n(= `IcosahedralIrrepDims` [1,3,3,4,5]): the angular-momentum levels\nrestrict as V₁ → T₁, V₂ → H, V₃ → T₂ ⊕ G.  This states *which* A₅\nirreps occur (not just the dimension bookkeeping already in\n`icos_branching_dim_check`): V₃'s dim-7 splits as the dim-3 T₂ plus the\ndim-4 G, the first level where two distinct icosahedral irreps co-occur. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.e8_dim_eq_rank_times_h_plus_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.e8_dim_eq_rank_times_h_plus_one","kind":"theorem","line":635,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L635-L637","doc":"dim E₈ = 248 = rank · (h + 1) = 8 · 31, with rank = 8 and Coxeter h = 30. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.order_2I_eq_four_times_coxeter","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.order_2I_eq_four_times_coxeter","kind":"theorem","line":629,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L629-L633","doc":"|2I| = 4 · h(E₈): the order of the McKay group is four times the\nCoxeter number (120 = 4 · 30). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.affineE8_marks_sum_eq_coxeter_30","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.affineE8_marks_sum_eq_coxeter_30","kind":"theorem","line":624,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L624-L627","doc":"The affine E₈ marks sum to the Coxeter number h(E₈) = 30\n(= dual Coxeter number h∨(E₈), E₈ being simply-laced). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedral_order_eq_120","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedral_order_eq_120","kind":"theorem","line":619,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L619-L622","doc":"|2I| = 120 by Burnside: Σ dim² over the 9 irreps = 1+4+9+16+25+36+16+4+9 = 120.\n(Matches |S₅| = 120, but 2I ≇ S₅ — see `spin_Z2_ne_sign_Z2`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedral_num_irreps","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedral_num_irreps","kind":"theorem","line":616,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L616-L617","doc":"2I has exactly 9 irreps (= number of affine E₈ nodes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedralIrrepDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binaryIcosahedralIrrepDims","kind":"def","line":612,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L612-L614","doc":"Dimensions of the 9 irreducible reps of the binary icosahedral group 2I,\nequal to the Coxeter marks of the affine E₈ Dynkin diagram (McKay). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reeb_eq_restriction_scaffold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.reeb_eq_restriction_scaffold","kind":"theorem","line":575,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L575-L596","doc":"**Reeb-thread = restriction functor (scaffold capstone, residual ii).**\nUnder the conjectural `BringFiberAction`, the geometric Reeb/fiber map and\nthe algebraic `Res^{S₅}_{S₃}` branching express the SAME conjugation\nsymmetry:\n(i) conjugate partitions share a fiber/icosahedral rotation (geometric,\n    `conjugate_same_a5_irrep`);\n(ii) their restriction content is sign-twisted (algebraic,\n    `restriction_intertwines_conjugation`);\n(iii) with the standard `(2,1)` carrier fixed (`std_irrep_conjugation_fixed`).\nThis is the scaffold-level \"Reeb = restriction\" identity that the\nBeasley–Witten Seifert–CS localization on `S³/2I` runs over — residual (ii)\nof `docs/audits/2026-06-20-keystone-wlambda-beasley-witten-localization.md`.\nThe `[BringFiberAction]` hypothesis is genuinely used (conjunct i). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.std_irrep_conjugation_fixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.std_irrep_conjugation_fixed","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L564-L573","doc":"**The standard `(2,1)` irrep is the conjugation-fixed carrier.**  The `S₃`\nsign-twist fixes the `(2,1)` multiplicity (3rd entry), so the load-bearing\nstandard irrep — which carries the Borromean `h⁴` per\n`restriction_functor_yields_h4_irrep` — sits in the conjugation-invariant\npart of every restriction, matching the Reeb fiber shared by conjugate\npartitions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.restriction_intertwines_conjugation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.restriction_intertwines_conjugation","kind":"theorem","line":550,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L550-L562","doc":"**Reeb = restriction (conjugation intertwiner).**  The `Res^{S₅}_{S₃}`\nbranching commutes with conjugation: restricting the conjugate partition\nequals sign-twisting the restriction,\n`Res(V_{λ'}) = Res(V_λ) ⊗ sgn_{S₃} = s3SignTwist(Res(V_λ))`.  This is the\nalgebraic shadow of the geometric `conjugate_same_a5_irrep` (conjugate\npartitions share a Reeb fiber): the shared Seifert-`S¹` fiber appears on the\n3-strand side as the `S₃` sign-twist intertwiner.  Both express the *same*\nconjugation symmetry — the scaffold-level content of \"the localization sum\nruns over the `Res^{S₅}_{S₃}` Bratteli branching\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3SignTwist","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3SignTwist","kind":"def","line":543,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L543-L548","doc":"The `S₃` sign-twist on a restriction-multiplicity triple `[m_triv, m_sign,\nm_std]`: tensoring by `sgn_{S₃}` swaps trivial ↔ sign and fixes standard.\nThis is the `S₃` shadow of the `S₅` conjugation (sign) involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSign_eq_w0_conj_sign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSign_eq_w0_conj_sign","kind":"theorem","line":508,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L508-L517","doc":"**`deltaSign = sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}})` explicitly.**  The hardcoded chirality table\nequals the longest-element sign `(-1)^{ℓ(w₀^{S_{λ'}})} = (-1)^{Σ_i C(λ'_i,2)}`\nof the conjugate Young subgroup — the form asserted in `deltaSign`'s\ndefinition.  Together with `nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj` and\n`deltaSign_eq_nStat_parity` this closes the loop\n`deltaSign = sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}}) = (-1)^{n(λ)}` (a-function / b-invariant parity),\nso the chirality sign is a forced cell invariant, not a table. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat_eq_sumChoose2_conj","kind":"theorem","line":500,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L500-L506","doc":"**`n(λ) = Σ_i C(λ'_i, 2)`** — the partition statistic equals the sum of\nbinomials over the **conjugate** partition's parts (the standard identity,\nhere verified at `n = 5`).  Since `Σ_i C(λ'_i,2) = ℓ(w₀^{S_{λ'}})`, this ties\n`nStat` to the conjugate Young subgroup's longest element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.sumChoose2","kind":"def","line":495,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L495-L498","doc":"`Σ_i C(μ_i, 2)` over a partition `μ`'s parts — the **length** `ℓ(w₀^{S_μ})` of\nthe longest element of the Young subgroup `S_μ = ∏_i S_{μ_i}` (each factor\n`S_{μ_i}` contributes `C(μ_i,2)` inversions). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjParts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjParts","kind":"def","line":485,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L485-L493","doc":"The conjugate (transpose) partition's parts, `λ' ⊢ 5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign_eq_nStat_parity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign_eq_nStat_parity","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L469-L483","doc":"**The Δ_λ chirality sign is the partition-statistic parity** — the PROBE-4\nre-scope (PR #2661).  The chirality sign equals `(-1)^{n(λ)}`, i.e. the parity\nof the b-invariant / Lusztig a-function — **not** an exogenous decoration.\nBecause the a-function is constant on Kazhdan–Lusztig cells, a *forced*\ncell-constant sign `(-1)^{a(w)}` factors through any nonnegative (KL)\nmultiplicity sum and reproduces this mixed-sign pattern; so the\nKL-positivity prune is re-scoped from \"the sign must be supplied exogenously\"\nto \"the sign **is** the a-function parity; the open Δ_λ problem is the\n*magnitude*\".  (`(-1)^{n(λ)} = sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}})`, the conjugate Young-subgroup\nlongest-element sign of `deltaSign`'s definition, for all `λ ⊢ n ≤ 8` per the\nsame probe; here proved at `n = 5`.)  See\n`docs/audits/2026-06-23-option-e-probe4-overturning-afunction-sign.md`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.nStat","kind":"def","line":459,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L459-L467","doc":"The partition statistic `n(λ) = Σ_i (i-1)·λ_i` (here the 0-indexed `Σ i·λ_i`\nover the enumerated parts, via a `(index, sum)` fold).  For the symmetric\ngroup this is the **b-invariant** (the lowest fake-degree exponent =\n`min_{T ∈ SYT(λ)} maj(T)`) and, since every `S_n` irrep is special, **Lusztig's\na-function** value on the two-sided cell of `V_λ`.  Verified combinatorially\n(b-invariant via min major index over SYT) in\n`docs/audits/scripts/option_e_probe4_overturning_afunction_sign.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.parts","kind":"def","line":449,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L449-L457","doc":"The partition of each `n = 5` block, as its weakly-decreasing list of parts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.electron_block","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.electron_block","kind":"theorem","line":443,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L443-L447","doc":"The electron block (3,1,1) is chirality-odd (deltaSign = -1), magnitude 6\n(self-conjugate partition; the T₁/T₂ split that carries the chirality). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSign_mixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.deltaSign_mixed","kind":"theorem","line":435,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L435-L441","doc":"**Mixed-sign** (the PROBE-4 KL-positivity-prune premise at n=5): both\nchirality signs occur, so no nonnegative (Kazhdan–Lusztig) weight can\nsupply the sign — the chirality must come from the parity twist, not a\npositive combination of dimensions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binding_magnitude_eq_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.binding_magnitude_eq_dim","kind":"theorem","line":430,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L430-L433","doc":"**Magnitude = Wedderburn dim**: |Δ_λ| = dim V_λ, i.e. (Δ_λ)² = (dim V_λ)². ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign_sq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign_sq_one","kind":"theorem","line":426,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L426-L428","doc":"Chirality is ±1 (deltaSign² = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaLambda","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaLambda","kind":"def","line":423,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L423-L424","doc":"The per-block binding factor Δ_λ = chirality sign × Wedderburn magnitude. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.deltaSign","kind":"def","line":413,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L413-L421","doc":"Δ_λ chirality sign = sgn(w₀^{S_{λ'}}) ∈ {±1}, computed per partition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3rot_branching_dim_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3rot_branching_dim_check","kind":"theorem","line":383,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L383-L394","doc":"**S₃-rotation branching dimension-consistency** (the analog of\n`icos_branching_dim_check` for the `s3RotBranchingMult` table, which until\nnow carried only the `s3_std_appears_at_ell1_and_ell2` spot-check).  For\neach angular-momentum level ℓ ≤ 4, the S₃⊂SO(3) rotation-subgroup\nmultiplicities partition the full dimension `2ℓ+1`:\n`Σ_μ (mult of μ in V_ℓ↓S₃) · dim(μ) = 2ℓ+1`.  The `length = 3` conjunct\nguards `List.zipWith` against silent truncation (cf. #2431). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_s3_restriction_dim_consistent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_s3_restriction_dim_consistent","kind":"theorem","line":367,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L367-L381","doc":"**Restriction dimension-consistency (the branching backbone).**  For every\npartition λ ⊢ 5, restricting V_λ to S_3 preserves total dimension:\n`Σ_μ (mult of μ in V_λ↓S_3) · dim(μ) = dim(V_λ)`.  This is the dimension\nbookkeeping that the S_5 → S_3 restriction functor `Res^{S_5}_{S_3}` must\nsatisfy (a vector space keeps its dimension on restriction, only its\ndecomposition changes), verifying `s5_to_s3_restriction_mults` against\n`PartitionOf5.dim` across all 7 blocks.  Because the count depends only on\nthe conjugacy class of the S_3 ⊂ S_5 subgroup, it is identical for the\nspacetime-frame-fixing embedding {1,2,3}↦{3,4,5} and the naive {1,2,3}↦\n{1,2,3} — the embedding-independence verified in\n`scripts/s5so3_branching_backbone_verify.py`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3IrrepDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3IrrepDims","kind":"def","line":363,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L363-L365","doc":"Dimensions of the 3 irreps of S_3, in the order\n[(3) trivial, (1,1,1) sign, (2,1) standard]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.restriction_functor_yields_h4_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.restriction_functor_yields_h4_irrep","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L350-L361","doc":"**Functor Resolution Theorem**: The load-bearing (2,1) irrep of H_3(q)\n(which carries the Borromean h^4 = -3/4 coefficient) appears with\nmultiplicity EXACTLY 2 in both the electron block (3,1,1) [ℓ=1] and the\nmuon block (3,2) [ℓ=2].\nThis validates the S_5 → S_3 restriction as the canonical functor connecting\nthe spherical-harmonic generation tower to the mass trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_s3_restriction_mults","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_to_s3_restriction_mults","kind":"def","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L338-L348","doc":"Branching multiplicities of the S_5 irreps under restriction to S_3.\nComputed via standard Littlewood-Richardson/Branching rules.\nOrder of S_3 irreps: [(3) trivial, (1,1,1) sign, (2,1) standard]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.spin_Z2_ne_sign_Z2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.spin_Z2_ne_sign_Z2","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L317-L327","doc":"**SU(2) double cover: spin ℤ₂ ≠ sign ℤ₂.**  The binary icosahedral group\n2I (the SU(2)-preimage of I ≅ A₅) has order 120 = |S₅|, but 2I is PERFECT\n(trivial abelianisation) while S₅ has abelianisation ℤ₂ (the sign\ncharacter).  Hence 2I ≇ S₅, and the spin ℤ₂ (SU(2)→SO(3) kernel) is a\ndifferent ℤ₂ from the sign ℤ₂ (S₅/A₅).  Encoded via the abelianisation\norders. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3_std_appears_at_ell1_and_ell2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3_std_appears_at_ell1_and_ell2","kind":"theorem","line":308,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L308-L315","doc":"The std/(2,1) irrep (which carries the Borromean h⁴) appears at BOTH ℓ=1\nand ℓ=2 under the S₃⊂SO(3) rotation embedding: multiplicities 1 and 2.\nTherefore \"S₃ sees only ℓ≤1\" is false — h⁴ cannot be attributed to \"ℓ=2\nonly\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3RotBranchingMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s3RotBranchingMult","kind":"def","line":295,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L295-L306","doc":"**The S₃-rotation-subgroup branching (corrects the source-file premise).**\nS₃ realised as the triangle-rotation subgroup of SO(3) (irreps triv,\nsign, std) branches `V_ℓ` with the std (=(2,1)) irrep already present at\nℓ=1 AND ℓ=2 — so the premise \"S₃ sees only ℓ≤1\" is FALSE.  Order:\n[triv, sign, std]. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ell2_yields_one_copy_of_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.ell2_yields_one_copy_of_H","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L283-L293","doc":"**The ℓ=2 reading.** The SO(3) angular-momentum level ℓ=2 restricts to\nEXACTLY ONE copy of the dim-5 icosahedral irrep H (the fifth entry), and\nH first appears at ℓ=2.  This is the derived \"ℓ=2 → dim-5 irrep\"\nstatement; it does NOT by itself supply the Borromean h⁴ coefficient\n(see audit: the h⁴ lives in the 3-strand H₃ algebra, a different\nrepresentation ring). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icos_branching_dim_check","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icos_branching_dim_check","kind":"theorem","line":274,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L274-L281","doc":"Dimension check: for each ℓ ≤ 6, `Σ mult·dim = 2ℓ+1`.  Confirms the\nicosahedral branching is consistent (the multiplicities partition the\nfull angular-momentum dimension). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icosBranchingMult","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.icosBranchingMult","kind":"def","line":261,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L261-L272","doc":"Multiplicity of each icosahedral irrep (in the order A, T₁, T₂, G, H)\ninside the restriction `V_ℓ|_I` of the SO(3) angular-momentum rep, as\nDERIVED from the I character table (probe output, ℓ = 0..6). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralIrrepDims","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralIrrepDims","kind":"def","line":258,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L258-L259","doc":"Dimensions of the five icosahedral (≅ A₅) irreps: A, T₁, T₂, G, H. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_so3_fiber_action_scaffold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.s5_so3_fiber_action_scaffold","kind":"theorem","line":226,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L226-L246","doc":"**Main statement (scaffold).** The S₅↔SO(3) fiber action on Bring's\nsurface gives a map from partition-wise Wedderburn data (S₅ irreps) to\nicosahedral spatial rotations (I ⊂ SO(3)), preserving the conjugation\nstructure.\n\nThe combinatorial half (dim² = 120, conjugation involutive) holds\nunconditionally.  Under the conjectural `BringFiberAction` the fiber map\nadditionally *identifies conjugate partitions* (same A₅ irrep ⇒ same\nrotation) — the corrected replacement for the falsified angle sign-flip,\nso the `[BringFiberAction]` hypothesis is genuinely used (not decorative).\n\nClosure of the open half requires the explicit `BringFiberAction` instance\nderived from Bring's quintic surface automorphism group (owner-gated step\n`conj:s5-so3-fiber-action`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.five_distinct_classes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.five_distinct_classes","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L223-L223","doc":"**Substantive** (de-vacuifying, replacing the prior `: True`): the five\nA₅ irreps realize five DISTINCT icosahedral conjugacy classes — five\ndistinct rotation angles.  A constant map fails injectivity, so this\ncannot be discharged vacuously (the falsified trivial instance is\nrejected). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.irrepToRotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.irrepToRotation","kind":"def","line":217,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L217-L217","doc":"The conjectural geometric fiber map on the corrected (A₅-irrep) domain:\neach A₅ irrep ↦ an icosahedral rotation, induced by Bring's quintic. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":214,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L214-L214","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.BringFiberAction","kind":"class","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L187-L224","doc":"**Class: fiber action of A₅ on Bring's surface (corrected domain).**\n\nThe conjectural content: the icosahedral action on Bring's quintic\nsurface Σ₄ induces a fiber map from the five A₅ irreps to icosahedral\nSO(3) rotations, realizing the A₅ irrep ↔ conjugacy-class duality.\n\nThis corrects the falsified `S₅-partition → rotation` map.  Per\n`docs/audits/2026-06-13-bring-fiber-action-falsification.md`, the prior\n7-partition domain made `respects_conjugate` (a geometric angle\nsign-flip `angle(λ') = -angle(λ)`) and `hits_five_conjugacy_classes`\n*mutually unsatisfiable* (orbit counting: 7 partitions ↦ 4 conjugation\norbits ↦ at most 4 classes), and the placeholder `: True` + trivial\ninstance discharged the class vacuously.  The corrected domain is the\nFIVE A₅ irreps (`A5Irrep`); the false sign-flip is replaced by the\ntheorem `PartitionOf5.conjugate_same_a5_irrep` (conjugate partitions\nshare a fiber — derived, not axiomatised).\n\nPer AGENTS.md §3b-cond the conjectural geometric map is a class field;\ndownstream results consume it via `[BringFiberAction]`.  The field\n`five_distinct_classes` is SUBSTANTIVE — a constant map fails injectivity\n— so the class is **not** vacuously satisfiable.  The explicit map\n(which A₅ irrep ↦ which icosahedral rotation, from Bring's quintic\nautomorphism group) is the open, owner-gated step\n`conj:s5-so3-fiber-action`; no global instance is provided, so downstream\ntheorems are genuinely conditional on it.\n\n-- Ref: [klein1888] Klein, Lectures on the Icosahedron (Bring) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedIcosahedralRotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedIcosahedralRotation","kind":"instance","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedIcosahedralRotation.default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedIcosahedralRotation.default","kind":"def","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L185-L185","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation.asSO3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation.asSO3","kind":"def","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L182-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L181-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.IcosahedralRotation","kind":"structure","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L177-L185","doc":"The icosahedral rotation group I as a subgroup of SO(3).\n|I| = 60 = |A_5|; the isomorphism A_5 ≅ I is the icosahedral\nsymmetry (Klein 1884).  This structure carries the abstract\ndata of an icosahedral rotation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedSO3Rotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedSO3Rotation","kind":"instance","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L175-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedSO3Rotation.default","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instInhabitedSO3Rotation.default","kind":"def","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L175-L175","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.angle","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.angle","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L174-L174","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_z","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_z","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L173-L173","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_y","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_y","kind":"def","line":172,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L172-L172","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_x","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.axis_x","kind":"def","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L171-L171","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation.mk","kind":"ctor","line":170,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L170-L170","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.SO3Rotation","kind":"structure","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L162-L175","doc":"A rotation in SO(3) about a given axis, by a given angle.\n\nBase ring (§7c): `ℝ` is intrinsic, not gratuitous — SO(3) is a real Lie\ngroup, the axis is a real 3-vector, and `angle` is a real rotation angle\n(compared for injectivity in `BringFiberAction.five_distinct_classes`, and\nthe archimedean home of the owner-gated geometric realization\n`conj:s5-so3-fiber-action`).  Do NOT generalize to a generic ring: a\n\"rotation axis\" over an arbitrary commutative ring is meaningless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate_same_a5_irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate_same_a5_irrep","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L152-L158","doc":"**Corrected conjugate-compatibility** (replaces the falsified geometric\nangle sign-flip `angle(λ') = -angle(λ)`): conjugate S₅-partitions restrict\nto the SAME A₅ irrep, hence share a fiber.  The sign-twist lives on the\nWedderburn/S₅ side, not as a geometric orientation reversal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.toA5Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.toA5Irrep","kind":"def","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L142-L150","doc":"The A₅ irrep each S₅ partition restricts to (its chirality\nrepresentative).  Conjugate partitions share an irrep; the self-conjugate\n(3,1,1) is sent to its T₁ representative (the T₁ ⊕ T₂ chirality split is\nrecorded in `s5_to_a5_electron_block_splits`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.card_eq_five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.card_eq_five","kind":"theorem","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L138-L140","doc":"A₅ has exactly five irreps — equal to its number of conjugacy classes\n(the character-table duality the fiber map realizes). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.dim","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L134-L136","doc":"Dimension of each A₅ irrep. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.allList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.allList","kind":"def","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L131-L132","doc":"All five A₅ irreps. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5Irrep.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5Irrep.repr","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprA5Irrep","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqA5Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqA5Irrep","kind":"instance","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L129-L129","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.H","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.G","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.T₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.T₂","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.T₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.T₁","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.A","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep.A","kind":"ctor","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L128-L128","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5Irrep","kind":"inductive","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L125-L129","doc":"The five irreducible representations of A₅ ≅ I (dims 1, 3, 3, 4, 5):\nA (trivial), the chirality pair T₁/T₂ (both dim 3), G (dim 4), H (dim 5). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_order_eq_60","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.A5_order_eq_60","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L108-L112","doc":"|A_5| = 60 by Burnside: 1² + 3² + 3² + 4² + 5² = 60. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.restrictsToA5Irrep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.restrictsToA5Irrep","kind":"def","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L91-L106","doc":"Indicator: which S_5 irreps restrict to non-trivial A_5 sub-reps\n(equivalently, which partitions are NOT self-conjugate AND have\ndifferent multiplicities under restriction).  The branching rule\nS_5 ↓ A_5 splits irreps whose conjugate-pair-mate is different,\nand keeps self-conjugate ones as-is.\n\nStandard rep theory: A_5 has 5 irreps of dim 1, 3, 3, 4, 5\n(totaling dim²-sum 1+9+9+16+25 = 60 = |A_5|). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.total_dim_squared_eq_120","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.total_dim_squared_eq_120","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L83-L86","doc":"Sum of dim² over partitions of 5 = |S_5| = 120 (Burnside / Wedderburn). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate_preserves_dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.conjugate_preserves_dim","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L77-L81","doc":"Conjugate partitions have equal dimensions (standard rep theory:\nsign-twist preserves dim, since χ_(λ')(g) = sgn(g) · χ_λ(g)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L72-L75","doc":"Conjugation is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.conjugate","kind":"def","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L61-L70","doc":"Conjugate partition (transpose Young diagram).  Pairs:\n(5) ↔ (1¹¹¹¹¹), (4,1) ↔ (2,1¹¹¹), (3,2) ↔ (2,2,1), (3,1,1) self-conjugate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.dim","kind":"def","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L50-L59","doc":"Dimension of the S_5 irrep V_λ for each partition λ ⊢ 5\n(standard hook-length formula values; cf. James 1984 §2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.allList","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.allList","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L46-L48","doc":"Explicit list of all 7 partitions of 5. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartitionOf5","kind":"instance","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartitionOf5.repr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instReprPartitionOf5.repr","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.instDecidableEqPartitionOf5","kind":"instance","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L44-L44","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.onesFive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.onesFive","kind":"ctor","line":43,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L43-L43","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.twoOneOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.twoOneOneOne","kind":"ctor","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L42-L42","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.twoTwoOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.twoTwoOne","kind":"ctor","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L41-L41","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.threeOneOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.threeOneOne","kind":"ctor","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L40-L40","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.threeTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.threeTwo","kind":"ctor","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L39-L39","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.fourOne","kind":"ctor","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L38-L38","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.five","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5.five","kind":"ctor","line":37,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L37-L37","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.PartitionOf5","kind":"inductive","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/S5SO3FiberAction.lean#L35-L44","doc":"Partitions of 5 (= 7 partitions, indexing the 7 irreps of S_5). ","signatureChunk":0}]}